**2. Wire it up in `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Add Problem Details support + custom handler
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<CustomExceptionHandler>();

var app = builder.Build();

// Must come before endpoint mapping
app.UseExceptionHandler();

app.MapGet("/example/{id}", (int id) =>
{
    if (id < 0) throw new ArgumentException("ID must be positive");
    if (id == 0) throw new KeyNotFoundException("Item not found");
    return Results.Ok(new { id });
});

app.Run();
```

**How it works:**

| Component | Role |
|-----------|------|
| `AddProblemDetails()` | Configures RFC 7807 content type (`application/problem+json`) |
| `AddExceptionHandler<T>()` | Registers your custom `IExceptionHandler` |
| `UseExceptionHandler()` | Adds the middleware that catches all unhandled exceptions |

**Key points:**
- No try-catch needed in endpoints — the middleware catches everything globally
- 500 responses suppress `exception.Message` to avoid leaking internals
- You can register multiple `IExceptionHandler` implementations (they chain in order)
- Return `false` from `TryHandleAsync` to pass to the next handler
